WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.266
While

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.900
in France,

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.501
people are

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.969
rallying for a third day

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.004
over the fatal police

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.405
shooting of a teenager.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.374
You are seeing his mother right there

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.708
leading a tribute march

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:09.642
a short while ago.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.343
The boy

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.878
identified by authorities

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:12.779
only as Nadal

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.047
and is reported

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.182
to be of North African descent.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.050
The shooting happened

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.985
during a traffic stop on Tuesday

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.020
in downtown

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.354
a working class town

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.556
on the outskirts of Paris.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.125
French officials say the officer

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.127
who shot and killed the 17 year

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.828
old acted, quote, illegally.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:29.696
We're now learning

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.031
that the officer has been put

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.465
under formal investigation

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.334
for voluntary homicide.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.268
Well, protesters

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.103
have set fire to several cars

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.038
in Old Town.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.639
French President Emmanuel Macron

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.641
calling the shooting unjustifiable

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.010
while also condemning the unrest.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.845
Our Paris correspondent Melissa Bell

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:46.346
has more

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.417
Cars, town

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:54.054
halls, schools set on fire across France

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.755
as rage over the police

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:59.192
shooting of 17 year old Niall continued

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.062
into his second night.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.930
Enough to force the French

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.932
president to call an emergency

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.867
ministerial meeting Listen.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:08.701
Did you know

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.336
the last hours have been marked

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:11.438
by violent scenes

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.906
against police stations,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.008
but also schools and town halls.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.776
And basically against institutions

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.877
and the republic.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.046
It's absolutely unjustifiable

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.548
just to share

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.918
the deployment of some 2000

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.486
police officers on Wednesday

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.887
to the Paris suburbs

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.023
did little to quell the anger

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.459
with 150 people detained

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.561
It's not the republic

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.862
that was in custody.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.297
It was not the republic

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.199
that killed this young man.

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:39.499
Please.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.201
The government's spokesman early

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.402
this morning

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.904
Another appeal in vain to calm

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.506
the violence has been described.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.108
Some of the attacks on government

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.609
institutions as

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.911
organized, almost coordinated

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.082
in response,

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:56.916
a massive

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.252
deployment of police forces on Thursday.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.688
Some 40,000 across France

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.157
including 5000 in Paris.

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.528
But even before nightfall, a protest

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.530
led by nuns mother turned violent.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.867
Emotions still raw

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.268
even as the police officer

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.302
accused of shooting.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.737
The teen was placed

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.305
under formal investigation

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:22.308
for voluntary homicide.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.776
Scuffles breaking out along

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:24.911
the margins of the march.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.613
Some 6000 strong,

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:29.115
according to local media.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.050
Anger on the streets

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.620
of France remains all too palpable,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.421
with a family grieving

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.557
and a community looking for answers

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:40.460
as Paris suburbs and much of the country

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.762
prepare for another difficult night

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.334
CNN's Melissa Bell standing by in Paris.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.536
And as I'm going to pick up

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:50.770
with what you left off there,

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.273
Melissa Community looking for answers.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.741
I'm expecting

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.075
that they will come out to the streets

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:56.910
once more.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.745
How are authorities preparing for this

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:01.848
Well, there are

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.249
those 40,000 policemen

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.451
and women that are to be deployed

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:08.188
not just here on the outskirts of Greater

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.322
Paris, Isa.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.124
And those neighborhoods,

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.458
those communities

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.594
so traditionally affected

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:17.564
by these sorts of incidents and questions

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.966
and tragedies

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:20.867
There is

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.802
the deployment across the country.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.103
But the fear is

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.973
that just as we saw last night,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.075
anything that represented the state,

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.944
whether it was schools,

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.946
police stations, town halls,

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.247
they were targeted.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.815
The expectation is that

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.717
that will happen again tonight

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:41.221
because of that deep seated anger

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:42.755
at the fact

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.592
that here in France for many years, Isa,

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.260
despite

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.363
many of these tragedies, over the years,

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.633
allegations of police brutality

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:57.337
and fears of the systemic racism

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:00.039
that many believe a fueled home

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:00.840
or allow them

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.942
or certainly have underpinned

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.178
them are not sufficiently investigated.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:05.511
In fact,

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.146
it is very difficult in this country

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.448
to find even the words to do

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:12.185
so since state institutions cannot speak

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:15.054
of questions of race and ethnicity in the

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.890
in the tradition, in the respect of the

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.059
institutions of the republic,

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.694
people are meant to be considered equal.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.564
What that means is that any hint

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.033
of differences that are to do with race

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.368
or religion or ethnicity

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.802
are sort of drowned out.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.204
And that's part of the frustration

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:32.205
that you're seeing

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.873
in those neighborhoods tonight.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.074
We saw it this afternoon.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.543
It's likely to continue tonight

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:38.911
because that anger

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.881
is something that they feel a great deal

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.416
and that they have a lot of trouble

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.351
getting recognized by authorities.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.219
And it has made it

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:47.520
traditionally very difficult

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.922
for the police to address

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.892
those issues of racism within its ranks.

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.128
We should be keeping a close eye

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:55.662
on what's happening

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:56.529
in the streets of Paris.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:57.130
Thank you very much.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.698
Melissa Bell there for us.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:04:59.232
Well, rights

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.233
groups in France

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.434
have been speaking out

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.935
against police violence

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.170
and systemic racism

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.872
within law enforcement for years.

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:07.540
I want to discuss further matter.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.776
This is an expert on security

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:10.843
and police issues,

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.045
as well as a political science

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:14.147
researcher at the University of Exile.

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.049
Matt, your great to have you on the show.

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.550
I mean, I want to get your thoughts

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.319
if I could start off with

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:20.620
with this tragic incident,

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.454
of course, that's fueled

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:23.222
this anger that Melissa was talking about

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.191
and this rage. It's fair.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.259
I think it's fair to say

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:27.694
that there's been a discrepancy

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:28.261
from what

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:30.229
the video of the traffic traffic

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.098
shop show and the police

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.299
initial statement.

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:34.300
What are your thoughts as

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.401
you looked at that video?

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.572
Well, there is indeed an

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:40.440
a discrepancy

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.041
between the initial statements

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.910
of the police officers

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.211
that said that

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.313
the car was about to hit them.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.382
And the reality, what the video shows.

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:52.051
Well, what I thought well, obviously,

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:54.387
it's not a self-defense case.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.321
It's not a self-defense

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.055
case in the sense

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:57.924
that I don't think

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:59.992
that the physical integrity

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:00.660
or lives

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.762
or the police officers were in danger

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:03.963
when they

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:06.265
when one of them decided to to fire

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.668
one rounds from his pistol.

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:13.506
My belief is that the defense

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:14.874
and basically

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:15.942
this is the statements

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:18.144
that the imprisoned police officer

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:21.414
that the one that is currently in custody

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:25.251
made is that the driving was of that

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.153
young man was extremely dangerous

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.488
and he was not supposed to be driving

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:30.556
in the first place because he's 17.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:30.857
In France,

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:31.791
you have to be 18 to

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:33.393
have a driver's license.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.560
And that he was posing

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.263
a danger of threats to the surrounding

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:39.098
potentially to surrounding people,

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:41.134
to bystanders, to people who were

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.568
working in the public space,

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.737
which is why he used

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:48.408
his firearm and in France since 2017

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:52.578
it is allowed to open fire on a vehicle

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:55.281
if that vehicle is basically fleeing

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:58.618
is not compliance and is posing a danger

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.487
to a physical danger to people around.

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:05.091
But you lay down the defense

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:06.893
which looks incredibly forward.

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:07.360
I mean it's not

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.828
reasons to be shooting someone

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:11.130
just because he's under age for driving.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.865
But you know, this is not mature.

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:14.400
And I think Melissa touched on this.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.936
This is not an isolated incident.

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:17.770
You know,

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.772
today chooses killing I should say,

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.474
was the third fatal

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:23.209
shooting during traffic stops in France

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:23.643
so far

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:27.914
in 2023 Last year there were a record 13.

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:29.882
I mean this suggests Mathieu doesn't it,

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.451
that there's something wrong

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:33.986
Yes.

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:34.954
This is why actually

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:37.457
I mentioned the 2017 law.

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:40.059
The 2017 law

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.296
caused a massive

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:45.565
increase of those of those shootings

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:50.002
before 2017 2016.

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:54.173
You had basically 120 or 130 shots

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:59.011
fired at vehicles in France in 2017.

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:01.280
The law was passed in early 2017.

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:04.116
That number increased to 202.

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:06.319
And indeed we went from basically

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:09.889
one to two people killed every year

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:12.725
during those incidents to above ten,

00:08:13.059 --> 00:08:15.528
which of course is much lower

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:16.329
than what it is

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:17.864
in the United States for instance.

00:08:17.864 --> 00:08:18.798
But by French

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:20.867
or even European standards,

00:08:20.867 --> 00:08:21.667
this is pretty high

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.135
if you compare with Germany.

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:26.038
Germany has almost none every year.

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:28.875
And the law clearly is a huge

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:30.176
part of the problem,

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:31.077
as you're stating

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:32.645
there were one parts of the problem.

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:33.312
The other is,

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:35.181
as I had several the protesters

00:08:35.181 --> 00:08:36.849
on our air say today,

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:38.217
they have been talking

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:41.354
about institutional racism and proof

00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:42.889
filing racial profile.

00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:43.956
One man said,

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:45.725
we are all night

00:08:45.725 --> 00:08:47.793
is all of us, I think was what he said

00:08:47.793 --> 00:08:49.762
is the French police

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:52.198
then force institutionally racist?

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:54.333
Okay.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:55.401
You're right.

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:57.803
This is part of the broader picture

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:59.939
and something that started

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:02.475
about 40 years ago.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.277
So basically

00:09:04.277 --> 00:09:05.778
for the international audience

00:09:05.778 --> 00:09:06.479
that is watching us,

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:08.915
you have to understand that

00:09:08.915 --> 00:09:12.318
French suburbs are on big urban areas.

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:14.387
In France, you have in the suburbs,

00:09:14.387 --> 00:09:16.122
